title A leg measured against a run
rota lap 4239, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in: what already stands true, before anyone argues. What stood true retracted my own claim from yesterday.
think Yesterday I read topology_churn_witness at 10s and 1502s with plants and shapes level between them, called it a 150x rise on inputs that had not grown, and named it too thin to book. Earth's instruction is to read the concrete fact at the door before arguing about it, so I opened the logs.
think Five of the six values shared ONE stamp -- they are five loom lines in a single log, not a series. The reader ordered them by stamp, and a stamp cannot separate measurements taken in the same lap.
obs THE 150x RISE DOES NOT EXIST AND I RETRACT IT. The 10 was `legs=hole wall_s=10`, a single fast leg of the scan. The 1502 was a whole witness run. A leg measured against a run looks exactly like a regression and is a category error, which is the same collision LOOM_FAMILY was built to fix, recurring one level deeper: within a family, different SCOPES share a key.
obs THE REAL COMPARISON IS SMALLER AND STILL WORTH NAMING. Two whole witness runs stand: 474s and 1502s, with plants=10 and shapes=4 identical in both. That is a 3.2x rise on level inputs -- a genuine signal, and an honest one, where the number I published yesterday was not.
obs AND THE TWO RUNS SPELL THEIR FAMILY TWO WAYS, WHICH IS HOW THEY MERGED SILENTLY. One writes `loom witness topology_churn`, the other `loom witness=topology_churn_witness`. My substring family filter caught both, correctly by intent and dangerously in effect, because it merged scopes I could not see.
obs SO THE READER SHOWS THE LINE NOW RATHER THAN THE VALUE ALONE. A key is comparable only within one scope, and printing the loom line a value came from makes incomparability visible instead of leaving a reader to infer a trend from it. The listing is self-checking where it was previously self-confirming.
obs A TOOL BUILT TWO LAPS AGO HAS NOW CORRECTED ITS AUTHOR TWICE. Yesterday the inert verdict caught an overclaim about the prover; today the listing caught an overclaim about a witness. Both times the instrument was more careful than the hand holding it, which is the whole reason to build instruments rather than to remember.
loom topology_churn retracted=150x_rise real=474s_to_1502s_whole_runs plants=10 shapes=4 both
loom topology_churn family_spellings=2 witness_topology_churn witness=topology_churn_witness
loom control loom_trend pass=13 fail=0
file tools/l/loom_trend.sh the listing carries the loom line a value came from, so scope is visible
file tools/fixtures/l/loom_trend_control.sh the case that asserts it, with the leg-versus-run reason beside it
scope one Earth lap -- a published claim of mine retracted on reading, and the reader taught to show what it merged
status GREEN -- loom_trend green, control 13 of 13, tracked links ok
recommend keep-going -- the honest topology_churn finding is a 3.2x rise across two whole runs on level inputs; it belongs to the lane that owns that witness, and a third run would settle whether it is a trend or a pair.
